WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.089 --> 00:00:04.380
The characters in the Final Destination franchise
really only have one way of protecting themselves

00:00:04.380 --> 00:00:08.410
when Death decides that it’s their time,
and that is to look for the signs and try

00:00:08.410 --> 00:00:09.460
to avoid them.

00:00:09.460 --> 00:00:13.080
Some of these signs, however, go unnoticed,
not only by the characters, but also by the

00:00:13.080 --> 00:00:14.809
majority of movie audiences.

00:00:14.809 --> 00:00:18.050
In the first minute of the opening credits,
there’s this weird keychain that leaves

00:00:18.050 --> 00:00:20.560
a shadow that looks like a man hanging by
the neck.

00:00:20.560 --> 00:00:24.039
This is how Death would eventually take out
Alex’s friend Tod who accidentally gets

00:00:24.039 --> 00:00:26.920
his neck wrapped around a bathroom clothesline.

00:00:26.920 --> 00:00:30.830
Shortly after, Alex is preparing to leave
for France and grabs his Touring France book.

00:00:30.830 --> 00:00:34.650
The next book behind it on the stack is Death
of a Salesman, which ends with an automobile

00:00:34.650 --> 00:00:38.763
induced death which is a sign about one of Final
Destination’s second main character, Terry.

00:00:38.763 --> 00:00:42.710
And no, that’s not a Death of a Salesman
spoiler, it’s in the title, OK?

00:00:42.710 --> 00:00:47.149
Then, the fan blows open the Touring France
book to A History Lesson page, where we see

00:00:47.149 --> 00:00:50.340
a picture of the gallows that were used in
France in the middle ages.

00:00:50.340 --> 00:00:54.320
The character Billy would also be executed
by beheading, when a piece of scrap metal

00:00:54.320 --> 00:00:55.890
shot out from under a train.

00:00:55.890 --> 00:00:59.970
And moments later, it flips to a page about
Jim Morrison’s tomb with the words, “This

00:00:59.970 --> 00:01:02.129
Is The End” graffitied onto it.

00:01:02.129 --> 00:01:05.789
Not only is this just a general omen about
death, but Jim Morrison actually died while

00:01:05.789 --> 00:01:09.969
in Paris, a fate shared with Carter at the
end of Final Destination.

00:01:09.969 --> 00:01:15.100
There would be many more signs, weird coincidences
that aren’t coincidences and hidden secrets

00:01:15.100 --> 00:01:19.849
in Final Destination, so stick around to the
end of this video to hear about the craziest

00:01:19.849 --> 00:01:20.832
one.

00:01:24.819 --> 00:01:28.450
Welcome to Things You Missed, this is a show
where I analyse all the hidden secrets and

00:01:28.450 --> 00:01:31.641
overlooked details in your favorite horror
films, and Final Destination 

00:01:31.641 --> 00:01:34.979
is going to be an interesting one to cover,
because the whole idea is that everything

00:01:34.979 --> 00:01:36.759
is Death’s design.

00:01:36.759 --> 00:01:40.810
“In death, there are no accidents.

00:01:40.810 --> 00:01:42.159
No coincidences.

00:01:42.159 --> 00:01:43.509
No mishaps.

00:01:43.509 --> 00:01:45.539
And no escapes.”

00:01:45.539 --> 00:01:49.299
So whenever there are weird little moments
of chance or details that may or may not be

00:01:49.299 --> 00:01:53.189
intentional, I might normally leave them off
the Things You Missed, or at least mention

00:01:53.189 --> 00:01:55.689
a disclaimer that I don’t know if they’re
intentional.

00:01:55.689 --> 00:01:59.560
But with Final Destination, we’ve already
been told not to doubt that these details

00:01:59.560 --> 00:02:00.560
are meaningful.

00:02:00.560 --> 00:02:05.409
So for example, Alex’s birthday is September
25th, 9/25, and the flight desk agent points

00:02:05.409 --> 00:02:08.149
out that his flight leaves at 9:25PM.

00:02:08.149 --> 00:02:13.269
But did you also notice his assigned seat
is in Row 25, Seat I, which is the ninth seat

00:02:13.269 --> 00:02:14.269
from the right?

00:02:14.269 --> 00:02:17.130
Did you notice the song Carter and Terry listen
to in the car?

00:02:17.130 --> 00:02:21.819
Into the Void is a track by the band Nine
Inch Nails; a song with exactly 25 lines.

00:02:21.819 --> 00:02:25.690
The lyrics of this song talk about the singer
trying to save himself, just like the characters

00:02:25.690 --> 00:02:26.690
in this movie.

00:02:26.690 --> 00:02:31.090
The first verse almost seems to line up perfectly
with what Alex goes through in the opening.

00:02:31.090 --> 00:02:33.090
Talking to myself all the way to the station.

00:02:33.090 --> 00:02:35.650
Pictures in my head of the Final Destination.

00:02:35.650 --> 00:02:38.040
All lined up, all the ones that aren't allowed
to stay.

00:02:38.040 --> 00:02:41.299
Tried to save myself but myself keeps slipping
away.

00:02:41.299 --> 00:02:43.900
We’re just scratching the surface of this,
get it?

00:02:43.900 --> 00:02:45.090
Cause Nine Inch Nails?

00:02:45.090 --> 00:02:46.090
Scratching the surface?

00:02:46.090 --> 00:02:47.650
I don’t like that joke either.

00:02:47.650 --> 00:02:50.120
Let’s get into the Things You Missed.

00:02:54.815 --> 00:02:58.890
Into the Void wasn’t the only song with
a deeper meaning in Final Destination.

00:02:58.890 --> 00:03:01.930
The one that comes up over and over is Rocky
Mountain High.

00:03:01.930 --> 00:03:05.269
We first hear it in the airport restroom,
where Alex makes the connection about the

00:03:05.269 --> 00:03:08.482
artist, John Denver, having died in a plane
crash.

00:03:11.482 --> 00:03:13.972
“John Denver.

00:03:18.973 --> 00:03:21.099
Died in a plane crash.”

00:03:21.099 --> 00:03:24.247
The opening line of that song speaks of a
27 year old.

00:03:25.460 --> 00:03:31.662
🎵 “He was born in the summer of his 27th
year.” 🎵

00:03:31.662 --> 00:03:36.200
Twenty-seven is the age that Jim Morrison,
who was referenced earlier, died in Paris.

00:03:36.200 --> 00:03:38.893
Another lyric mentions a fire in the sky.

00:03:38.893 --> 00:03:42.908
🎵 “I’ve seen it raining fire in the
sky.” 🎵

00:03:42.908 --> 00:03:46.379
...which is what witnesses saw during the
explosion on Flight 180.

00:03:46.379 --> 00:03:49.889
This song becomes an omen of death for those
who got off the plane.

00:03:49.889 --> 00:03:52.587
Tod momentarily plugs in a radio before his
death.

00:03:54.803 --> 00:03:59.672
🎵 Colorado Rocky Mountain high! 🎵

00:03:59.672 --> 00:04:03.180
Ms. Lewton puts on the record before her final
moments.

00:04:03.180 --> 00:04:07.279
🎵 Rocky Mountain High - John Denver 🎵

00:04:07.279 --> 00:04:11.461
And in the final scene, a street performer
covers the song in French.

00:04:16.746 --> 00:04:20.500
Outside of music, there are other things that
connect each of the accidents.

00:04:20.500 --> 00:04:23.900
Since the seven who got off the plane were
supposed to die on route to France there are

00:04:23.900 --> 00:04:27.240
many references to the country of France seen in each
disaster scene.

00:04:27.240 --> 00:04:29.310
Let’s call them The French Connections.

00:04:29.310 --> 00:04:32.720
For context, that is a better joke than the
one I made earlier, but only slightly.

00:04:32.720 --> 00:04:34.270
I’ll start with the plane.

00:04:34.270 --> 00:04:38.670
Flight 180’s aircraft has blue, white and
red stripes reminiscent of the French flag.

00:04:38.670 --> 00:04:40.180
Makes sense, it’s a French airline.

00:04:40.180 --> 00:04:44.270
But that doesn’t explain, why the bus that
hits Terry has blue white and red stripes,

00:04:44.270 --> 00:04:48.620
or why the train that crashes into Carter’s
car is also lined with blue, white and red.

00:04:48.620 --> 00:04:52.470
It might also be worth mentioning that Billy is
also seen wearing blue, white and red on a

00:04:52.470 --> 00:04:53.470
couple of occasions.

00:04:53.470 --> 00:04:57.229
When we first meet him he’s got on a Rangers
jersey and in the scene where he is decapitated,

00:04:57.229 --> 00:04:59.810
he has a flannel with blue, white and red
stripes.

00:04:59.810 --> 00:05:03.199
Outside of the French flags, there are other
France and Paris references.

00:05:03.199 --> 00:05:07.120
In the airport, the only other Paris flight
that night is cancelled, and in the terminal,

00:05:07.120 --> 00:05:11.290
Clear is reading Tropic of Cancer by Henry
Miller, which was notably written in France.

00:05:11.290 --> 00:05:14.960
The room they are moved to after the crash
has clocks for several cities across the globe,

00:05:14.960 --> 00:05:17.120
but the one we see on screen is Paris.

00:05:17.120 --> 00:05:20.560
When Death comes for Clear at the climax of
the movie, she burns a candle for light, and

00:05:20.560 --> 00:05:25.150
we see four miniature Eiffel Towers, and when
Clear and Alex grab coffee together they sit

00:05:25.150 --> 00:05:29.569
outdoors in a cafe, clearly inspired by the
street corner cafes that dominate much of

00:05:29.569 --> 00:05:30.860
the city of Paris.

00:05:30.860 --> 00:05:34.550
At the end of the movie, they sit and have
a drink at a real French cafe, moments before

00:05:34.550 --> 00:05:38.721
Death makes an attempt on Alex and Carter
before the movie ends, which is teached at

00:05:38.721 --> 00:05:43.819
by a few interesting books seen on Ms. Lewton’s
bookshelf, most notably End Game In Paris.

00:05:43.819 --> 00:05:48.069
The teacher’s bookshelf also had some other
interesting titles, that can lead us to discover

00:05:48.069 --> 00:05:49.430
even more secrets.

00:05:58.560 --> 00:06:01.970
One of the other book titles on Ms. Lewton’s
shelf that I found to maybe have a deeper

00:06:01.970 --> 00:06:06.770
meaning was “The Cradle Will Fall”, a
1980 novel by Mary Higgins Clark.

00:06:06.770 --> 00:06:10.740
Perhaps this title is a reference to the unusually
high number of young high school kids aboard

00:06:10.740 --> 00:06:13.020
Flight 180 when it fell out of the sky.

00:06:13.020 --> 00:06:16.169
Or perhaps a reference to that fact that there
was a baby on board the flight?

00:06:16.169 --> 00:06:19.889
Also, why has there not been a Final Destination
movie where the victims are all babies?

00:06:19.889 --> 00:06:23.800
Like a hospital nurse has a vision that helps
her prevent a gas leak in the nursery, and

00:06:23.800 --> 00:06:27.500
now Death is coming for all these newborns
and the parents have to protect their kids

00:06:27.500 --> 00:06:28.600
from a series of disasters?

00:06:28.600 --> 00:06:31.740
It would be the ultimate horror movie for
first time parents.

00:06:31.740 --> 00:06:33.720
The other book that Ms. Lewton has is called
“Heads.”

00:06:33.720 --> 00:06:37.000
I’m sure you can find the significance behind
that one on your own.

00:06:37.000 --> 00:06:40.659
You may have also noticed Ms. Lewton’s first
name.

00:06:40.659 --> 00:06:43.321
“Hi, this is Valerie Lewton I need Agent
Shrek.”

00:06:43.321 --> 00:06:46.900
“Are you talking to… me?”

00:06:47.319 --> 00:06:52.000
Ms. Valerie Lewton is a reference to Val Lewton,
one of the most prolific horror film producers,

00:06:52.000 --> 00:06:54.650
who made classics like Cat People, I Walked
With A Zombie, and…

00:06:54.650 --> 00:06:56.400
The Seventh Victim.

00:06:56.400 --> 00:07:00.040
There are seven victims that Death comes for
after escaping Flight 180.

00:07:00.040 --> 00:07:03.569
There are other characters whose names pay
homage to classic horror icons.

00:07:03.569 --> 00:07:07.360
The other French teacher was named Mr. Murnau,
after FW Murnau.

00:07:07.360 --> 00:07:11.710
Terry Chaney was named for Lon Chaney, Alex
Browning for Tod Browning (and by the way

00:07:11.710 --> 00:07:15.590
Alex’s friend Tod spells his name with one
D, just like Tod Browning did), Tod’s brother

00:07:15.590 --> 00:07:20.180
is named George Waggner, named directly after
George Waggner, Blake Dreyer for Carl Theodor

00:07:20.180 --> 00:07:24.909
Dreyer and Billy Hitchcock for Alfred Hitchcock,
the director of films like Strangers on a

00:07:24.909 --> 00:07:28.500
Train (Billy is killed by a train) and The
39 Steps.

00:07:28.500 --> 00:07:32.539
There are 39 people from Mt Abraham High School
who died on Flight 180.

00:07:32.539 --> 00:07:36.840
The survivors meet with investigators 39 minutes
after the departure time and the memorial

00:07:36.840 --> 00:07:39.120
is held 39 days after the accident.

00:07:39.120 --> 00:07:42.590
Tod dies at 10:39PM and Ms. Lewton dies at
home.

00:07:42.590 --> 00:07:43.820
Her street address?

00:07:43.820 --> 00:07:44.820
39.

00:07:44.820 --> 00:07:46.379
The memorial statue is a bird.

00:07:46.379 --> 00:07:48.830
The Volée 180 victims died while in flight.

00:07:48.830 --> 00:07:52.500
I don’t know if this is coincidence, or
the intention of the person who designed the

00:07:52.500 --> 00:07:55.380
statue, but like I mentioned at the beginning
of this video, I’m not gonna worry about

00:07:55.380 --> 00:07:57.180
that as long as I’m covering Final Destination.

00:07:57.180 --> 00:08:01.430
Of course, while 39 did pass away, there were
7 survivors.

00:08:01.430 --> 00:08:05.520
After Terry’s death, the number 7 is splattered
onto Alex’s cheek in blood, and he was scheduled

00:08:05.520 --> 00:08:08.150
to be last on Death’s list -- he was #7.

00:08:08.150 --> 00:08:11.879
Thirty-nine lost plus seven survived equals
46 total on the field trip.

00:08:11.879 --> 00:08:13.870
The flight takes off out of Gate 46.

00:08:13.870 --> 00:08:16.389
Alex’s address is 4688.

00:08:16.389 --> 00:08:19.939
On the topic of Flight 180, the trip is booked
on Volée Airlines.

00:08:19.939 --> 00:08:22.280
Volée is a French word meaning “stolen”.

00:08:22.280 --> 00:08:25.159
Alex and the others have stolen additional
time from Death.

00:08:25.159 --> 00:08:28.400
One of the other things in the opening credits
is when the wind blows and this book flips

00:08:28.400 --> 00:08:33.320
through pages on the Devil, Evil, Damnation
and other topics, including a photo of someone

00:08:33.320 --> 00:08:37.990
holding a cross to the devil, the same way
a fourth quarter lead up to the Atlanta Falcons.

00:08:37.990 --> 00:08:41.900
Then, when Alex boards the aircraft, he looks
down and sees a luggage cart with the number

00:08:41.900 --> 00:08:44.000
of the devil: 666.

00:08:44.000 --> 00:08:47.970
After that, the series doesn’t really make
mention of anything demonic, instead, just

00:08:47.970 --> 00:08:51.820
focusing on The Grim Reaper, but as more of
a natural force than an entity.

00:08:51.820 --> 00:08:55.510
But I wonder if the demonic imagery at the
beginning is a suggestion that those who try

00:08:55.510 --> 00:08:58.220
to cheat death would be confined to hell.

00:08:58.220 --> 00:09:06.390
“Disrespecting the design could incite a
fury that could terrorize even the grim reaper.”

00:09:06.390 --> 00:09:09.030
On the other end of the spectrum from the
Devil, is God.

00:09:09.030 --> 00:09:12.980
In Alex's room, there’s a poster that reads:
“At one point he wanted to become a priest.

00:09:12.980 --> 00:09:14.650
He settled for being a God.

00:09:14.650 --> 00:09:19.500
I believe that’s a photo a Babe Ruth, and
with a career OPS of 1.164, I’ve got to

00:09:19.500 --> 00:09:20.500
agree with the poster.

00:09:20.500 --> 00:09:23.760
Of course, Alex lives on Long Island, New
York, and it’s even mentioned that he and

00:09:23.760 --> 00:09:27.880
Tod are Yankee fans, so this poster makes
sense, but is it a sign of things to come

00:09:27.880 --> 00:09:28.820
for Alex?

00:09:28.820 --> 00:09:33.069
ALEX: “If I see it, then I intervene, and if
I intervene, I change the design.”

00:09:33.069 --> 00:09:34.871
CARTER: “What? Intervene? What are you God now?”

00:09:35.872 --> 00:09:37.840
ALEX: “God’s not afraid to die.

00:09:37.840 --> 00:09:39.520
Gods don’t die.

00:09:39.520 --> 00:09:40.640
We do.”

00:09:40.640 --> 00:09:44.670
Maybe Alex’s awareness about his mortality
is also the reason he can’t stop focusing

00:09:44.670 --> 00:09:46.320
on the word “Terminal” at the airport.

00:09:46.320 --> 00:09:49.710
Or maybe that’s just another side effect
of his clairvoyant abilities.

00:09:49.710 --> 00:09:53.200
There are actually many more signs about the
fate of each character that Death comes for

00:09:53.200 --> 00:09:54.830
outside of the ones I’ve already mentioned.

00:09:54.830 --> 00:09:59.130
The night of the plane crash, Alex sees lightning
strike his street, and at the cabin, lightning

00:09:59.130 --> 00:10:00.430
shoots out of his lighter.

00:10:00.430 --> 00:10:03.910
These are both clues about the storm that
nearly took Clear’s life later on.

00:10:03.910 --> 00:10:07.600
The coroner explains that every move we make
is part of Death’s design, and one of the

00:10:07.600 --> 00:10:10.900
examples he uses is “the red light we stop
at, or run.”

00:10:10.900 --> 00:10:15.270
Then, not long after Alex uses a similar example
while trying to explain his theory.

00:10:15.270 --> 00:10:18.270
He says that crossing an intersection could
lead to death.

00:10:18.270 --> 00:10:21.480
Sure enough, Terry’s death is the result
of a run light in an intersection.

00:10:21.480 --> 00:10:25.840
It happens shortly after Clear tells Alex,
“You can find death omens anywhere you want

00:10:25.840 --> 00:10:29.060
to,” and he looks up to see the reflection
of a bus that isn’t really there.

00:10:29.060 --> 00:10:30.840
The next victim is Ms. Lewton.

00:10:30.840 --> 00:10:35.790
After she gets done packing the codpiece that
she has… for some reason… she’s attacked

00:10:35.790 --> 00:10:39.600
by an exploding computer monitor and falls
against the stained glass window with an image

00:10:39.600 --> 00:10:43.600
of a dagger, foreshadowing the knife she ultimately
ends up getting stabbed with.

00:10:43.600 --> 00:10:47.230
Alex realizes something is wrong when he’s
walking outside and sees a neighbor burning

00:10:47.230 --> 00:10:48.490
a pile of leaves.

00:10:48.490 --> 00:10:52.160
This was his sign that Ms. Lewton would accidentally
start a fire inside her home.

00:10:52.160 --> 00:10:56.020
And when that fire is ignited, there’s a
moving box in the background, made by a brand

00:10:56.020 --> 00:10:57.550
called “Shadow Transfer.”

00:10:57.550 --> 00:11:02.170
In this movie, Death is never seen, but sometimes
a shadow casts over them, and whenever a character

00:11:02.170 --> 00:11:06.040
passes away or evades Death, the target is
transferred on to the next person.

00:11:06.040 --> 00:11:09.820
There is also a set order -- the survivors
are supposed to die in the same order they

00:11:09.820 --> 00:11:11.870
would have gone out in during the plane crash.

00:11:11.870 --> 00:11:16.120
Like the dominos on coffee table in Alex’s
home, they are set up to fall in order.

00:11:16.120 --> 00:11:19.100
That’s how Alex knows that Ms. Lewton is
going to be next after Terry.

00:11:19.100 --> 00:11:22.740
He goes into the house, makes sure to leave
behind his fingerprint on the murder weapon

00:11:22.740 --> 00:11:24.420
and his shoeprint on the floor.

00:11:24.420 --> 00:11:25.420
MOVIE CHARACTERS.

00:11:25.420 --> 00:11:26.640
WHY ARE YOU LIKE THIS?

00:11:26.640 --> 00:11:28.860
At least wipe it down afterwards.

00:11:28.860 --> 00:11:29.860
You know what?

00:11:29.860 --> 00:11:32.180
I need to save my yelling voice for the second
and fourth ones.

00:11:32.180 --> 00:11:33.290
Next in line is Carter.

00:11:33.290 --> 00:11:36.640
Death’s plan for him is a collision with
a train, because these movies are all about

00:11:36.640 --> 00:11:39.020
Planes, Trains and Automobiles....

00:11:39.020 --> 00:11:40.290
And Shrek.

00:11:40.290 --> 00:11:42.990
“This is Agent Shrek.”

00:11:42.990 --> 00:11:43.990
🎵 Shrekophone 🎵

00:11:43.990 --> 00:11:49.110
But when Alex sees the premonition about the
train, he sees train number 747, which links

00:11:49.110 --> 00:11:53.580
back to the type of aircraft they narrowly
escaped in the opening, a Boeing 747.

00:11:53.580 --> 00:11:57.371
Finally, when Alex, Clear and Carter think
it’s over, and they’ve survived, Clear

00:11:57.371 --> 00:12:01.440
spills her wine on the able and Alex’s name
on the airport seating chart looks as if it

00:12:01.440 --> 00:12:05.000
is stained in blood, and that’s when he
knows… that he should stay tuned, because

00:12:05.000 --> 00:12:07.475
we’ve got even more hidden details to uncover…

00:12:16.880 --> 00:12:21.460
After surviving the disastrous Volée Flight
180, Alex becomes obsessed with learning how

00:12:21.460 --> 00:12:25.920
the crash might have occured on a technical
level, collecting books, manuals and newspapers

00:12:25.920 --> 00:12:27.270
to learn as much as possible.

00:12:27.270 --> 00:12:31.140
He comes across an article about the memorial
service held at his school and the author

00:12:31.140 --> 00:12:33.910
of the article is a reference to the Art Department
Coordinator of the movie.

00:12:33.910 --> 00:12:36.970
There’s also an article on the side written
by the assistant art director.

00:12:36.970 --> 00:12:41.080
Another newspaper headlines: High School Teacher
Dies In Mysterious Blaze, and a nearby article

00:12:41.080 --> 00:12:43.330
is authored by another member of the art department.

00:12:43.330 --> 00:12:46.760
There easter eggs, which I’ve come to call
“crew reference easter eggs” are seen

00:12:46.760 --> 00:12:50.930
in a lot of movies, but Final Destination
might be record setter, at least as far as

00:12:50.930 --> 00:12:53.190
the movies I’ve covered here on Things You
Missed go.

00:12:53.190 --> 00:12:57.270
Most of it is thanks to the Flight 180 memorial
itself, where all but a few of the listed

00:12:57.270 --> 00:13:01.110
victims are just random names who worked on
Final Destination, so rather, than reading

00:13:01.110 --> 00:13:04.380
them all out, you can just pause the video
if you want to see them for yourself.

00:13:04.380 --> 00:13:08.510
The only other notable crew reference easter
egg can be found outside Ms. Lewton’s house.

00:13:08.510 --> 00:13:12.380
As you know, she’s planning on moving away,
so she has a realtor sign in her yard, and

00:13:12.380 --> 00:13:16.400
it looks like the name of the realtor is C
Kristen, whereas the actual actress that plays

00:13:16.400 --> 00:13:18.160
Ms. Lewton is a Kristen C.

00:13:18.160 --> 00:13:22.000
In this video, I’ve focused a lot on the
signs of impending death, but there may also

00:13:22.000 --> 00:13:23.510
be clues about future relationships.

00:13:23.510 --> 00:13:27.660
I mean, the obvious one is when Alex pulls
out the Penthouse Magazine immediately after

00:13:27.660 --> 00:13:31.640
seeing the photo of Clear in the newspaper,
I mean I always thought that was a weird thing

00:13:31.640 --> 00:13:35.370
to include in the movie, that’s just his
immediate reaction, but the less obvious one

00:13:35.370 --> 00:13:39.090
would be towards the end, when he’s trying
to save her life in the lightning storm.

00:13:39.090 --> 00:13:42.460
Clear is trapped in the car and they’re
separated by the window as he tries to tell

00:13:42.460 --> 00:13:43.460
her what to do.

00:13:43.460 --> 00:13:46.530
In the corner of the window, there’s a little
bit of pro-seatbelt propaganda, showing the

00:13:46.530 --> 00:13:50.840
buckle and the release with the words: Get
Together, which is exactly what Alex and Clear

00:13:50.840 --> 00:13:55.030
do sometime during the six month time gap
before the final scene in Paris.

00:13:55.030 --> 00:13:58.470
But before we get to that final scene, there
is one more pattern that I have to point out,

00:13:58.470 --> 00:14:02.250
because it continues on into all the Final
Destination sequels so far.

00:14:02.250 --> 00:14:06.640
Every disaster scene in the movie, is somehow
connected to water. Or at least liquid.

00:14:06.640 --> 00:14:09.560
The first example is the least obvious, the
plane crash.

00:14:09.560 --> 00:14:13.030
If you’re familiar with the geography, this
makes sense, but even if you aren’t you’ll

00:14:13.030 --> 00:14:16.690
find out later in the movie that the plane
crashed into the ocean, somewhere beyond Jones

00:14:16.690 --> 00:14:21.260
Beach, which is where Alex goes to hide out
and ponder the possibilities of other dimensions.

00:14:21.260 --> 00:14:25.040
Next is the Tod strangulation scene, which
is obviously caused when he slips on the leaked

00:14:25.040 --> 00:14:26.040
toilet water.

00:14:26.040 --> 00:14:29.640
Side note, this is the only disaster scene
in the series that really seems to suggest

00:14:29.640 --> 00:14:33.470
there is something supernatural at play, because
of the way the water recedes after Tod’s

00:14:33.470 --> 00:14:34.830
name is added to the body count.

00:14:34.830 --> 00:14:38.900
I tried finding the scene YouTube to see if
anyone had any interesting takes on this,

00:14:38.900 --> 00:14:43.500
but all I found was our man Jhonwil from 10
years ago saying, “The way those green liquid

00:14:43.500 --> 00:14:46.310
substance go on towards him really scares
me…”

00:14:46.310 --> 00:14:51.469
So, all I learned was basically what I already
knew: that I love reading the YouTube comments.

00:14:51.469 --> 00:14:56.620
Terry's death happens while they're getting drinks, so not a lot to say there. I mean, this time the liquid is coffee rather than water.

00:14:56.620 --> 00:14:59.680
Ms. Lewton’s disaster scene is next, and
it all starts with her boiling water, which

00:14:59.680 --> 00:15:03.610
ends up being replaced with vodka, which seeps
out of her mug and into the the computer monitor,

00:15:03.610 --> 00:15:05.937
which somehow makes the monitor explode.

00:15:08.190 --> 00:15:12.290
The next disaster is the one at the railroad
tracks, where Carter avoids Death, but Billy,

00:15:12.290 --> 00:15:13.700
the next in line, does not.

00:15:13.700 --> 00:15:17.410
It’s dark out, so it’s a bit hard to see
when it happens, but it is raining during

00:15:17.410 --> 00:15:18.410
this scene.

00:15:18.410 --> 00:15:20.040
It’s a little bit more obvious when they’re in
the car shortly before.

00:15:20.040 --> 00:15:24.160
This, of course, is the last one before the
big lightning storm that was supposed to take

00:15:24.160 --> 00:15:25.160
out Clear.

00:15:25.160 --> 00:15:28.620
Obviously, there’s a bunch of water in this
one: the rain, the fact that Alex travels

00:15:28.620 --> 00:15:32.130
to her house in a canoe in the middle of a
lightning storm (which, in any other movie

00:15:32.130 --> 00:15:35.840
would be the dumbest idea in the movie, but
in Final Destination, we’ll just call it

00:15:35.840 --> 00:15:39.300
ONE of the dumbest ideas in the movie) and
then Alex almost gets the David Dunn treatment

00:15:39.300 --> 00:15:40.170
from a tree,

00:15:42.911 --> 00:15:45.390
...and then there's the whole thing with the pool flooding the area,

00:15:45.390 --> 00:15:47.479
so really this one is filled
with water. 

00:15:47.479 --> 00:15:51.050
There are also other water connections that
aren’t necessarily part of the disasters,

00:15:51.050 --> 00:15:55.180
like when Alex is having his “alone time”
with the magazine, the model is standing in

00:15:55.180 --> 00:15:59.000
the water, then there’s a part where Clear
and Alex put Alka Seltzer in their water glasses

00:15:59.000 --> 00:16:03.360
at the exact same time (maybe another clue
about their upcoming relationship), and just the girl’s

00:16:03.360 --> 00:16:06.430
name: Clear Rivers, it’s one of the wateriest
names I’ve ever heard.

00:16:06.430 --> 00:16:09.410
So that finally takes us to the big conclusion
in Paris.

00:16:09.410 --> 00:16:13.450
We can see that the ground is wet, and I already
mentioned Clear’s spilled drink, so the

00:16:13.450 --> 00:16:18.640
water / liquid theme is still there, but the
BIG connection can be seen after that.

00:16:18.640 --> 00:16:22.330
Alex narrowly avoids getting hit by a bus,
which swerves into a lamppost, which knocks

00:16:22.330 --> 00:16:26.030
loose the sign for this restaurant, Le Cafe
Miro 81.

00:16:26.030 --> 00:16:29.840
Carter miraculously saves him from getting
hit by the sign, but when it swings back around

00:16:29.840 --> 00:16:33.310
towards them, we’re seeing the backside
of the broken off portion of the sign, giving

00:16:33.310 --> 00:16:35.410
it the appearance of 180.

00:16:35.410 --> 00:16:38.600
Volée Flight 180 was not done with them yet.

00:16:38.600 --> 00:16:42.500
I’m gonna be covering the entire Final Destination
franchise, so look out for the next episode

00:16:42.500 --> 00:16:44.810
of Things You Missed in that playlist on the
left.

00:16:44.810 --> 00:16:48.840
If you love horror remember to subscribe to
CZsWorld for new horrors every week, ring

00:16:48.840 --> 00:16:53.120
the deathbell to select all notifications
and I’ll see you in the next one.

00:16:53.120 --> 00:16:55.376
Assuming we both survive.

00:16:55.376 --> 00:16:59.504
If you want to beat death, I recommend a facemask
and social distancing.

